{"units": [{"id": "pothen-word3", "translation": "From where do you have rushing, god-bearing [things]?"}, {"id": "pothen-word4", "translation": "From where do you have the boundaries of the divine road?"}, {"id": "pothen-word5", "translation": "From where will you have a feast of a like hand?"}, {"id": "pothen-word6", "translation": "From what country is the stranger?"}, {"id": "pothen-word7", "translation": "From where?"}, {"id": "pothen-word8", "translation": "From where would there be for me of the upper air?"}, {"id": "pothen-word9", "translation": "From where did he send libations? From what [source]?"}, {"id": "pothen-word10", "translation": "Πλούρα δε ηοχ υσυ διχι εν Θες. βολ. 6 π"}, {"id": "pothen-enclitic-orth1", "translation": "from somewhere"}, {"id": "pothen-enclitic-def1", "translation": "from somewhere"}, {"id": "pothen-enclitic-note1", "translation": "enclitic"}, {"id": "pothen-enclitic-note2", "translation": "Φα-νεὶς ἀλάστωρ ἢ κακὸς δαίμων [appearing as an avenger or evil spirit]"}, {"id": "pothen-enclitic-note3", "translation": "Νῦν δ᾽ [but now]"}, {"id": "pothen-enclitic-note4", "translation": "Ταυρό-φθογγοι δ᾽ ὑπομυκῶνται ποθὲν ἐξ ἀφανοῦς [and bull-voiced [things] bellow from somewhere out of the unseen]"}, {"id": "pothen-enclitic-quote1", "translation": "from somewhere"}, {"id": "pothen-enclitic-quote2", "translation": "a third savior came from somewhere"}, {"id": "pothen-enclitic-quote3", "translation": "fearful imitators"}, {"id": "pothen-enclitic-word1", "translation": "appearing as an avenger or evil spirit"}, {"id": "pothen-enclitic-word2", "translation": "but now"}, {"id": "pothen-enclitic-word3", "translation": "and bull-voiced [things] bellow from somewhere out of the unseen"}, {"id": "potheo-orth1", "translation": "to desire"}, {"id": "potheo-def1", "translation": "I desire"}, {"id": "potheo-note1", "translation": "Τοῦτο γὰρ [for this]"}, {"id": "potheo-note2", "translation": "Ποθοῦσαν φιλτάτην ήβην [longing for dearest youth]"}, {"id": "potheo-note3", "translation": "Περσίδες ἀνδρῶν [Persian women of men]"}, {"id": "potheo-note4", "translation": "Καὶ μὴν ἄλλον γε [and indeed another]"}, {"id": "potheo-note5", "translation": "Ποθεῖν [to long for]"}, {"id": "potheo-note6", "translation": "Ποθεῖν [to long for]"}, {"id": "potheo-quote1", "translation": "I long for"}, {"id": "potheo-quote2", "translation": "of the land"}, {"id": "potheo-quote3", "translation": "longing to see the new union"}, {"id": "potheo-quote4", "translation": "we long for"}, {"id": "potheo-quote5", "translation": "things that are not right"}, {"id": "potheo-quote6", "translation": "Do you mean the army longing for this land?"}, {"id": "potheo-word1", "translation": "for this"}, {"id": "potheo-word2", "translation": "longing for dearest youth"}, {"id": "potheo-word3", "translation": "Persian women of men"}, {"id": "potheo-word4", "translation": "and indeed another"}, {"id": "potheo-word5", "translation": "to long for"}, {"id": "potheo-word6", "translation": "to long for"}, {"id": "pothos-orth1", "translation": "longing, desire"}, {"id": "pothos-def1", "translation": "longing, desire"}, {"id": "pothos-def2", "translation": "Πόθος [Longing] Cupid."}, {"id": "pothos-note1", "translation": "Ὡς ἂν τὸ Δῖον ὄμμα [so that the divine eye]"}, {"id": "pothos-note2", "translation": "Πόθῳ [with longing]"}, {"id": "pothos-note3", "translation": "Λέκτρα δ᾽ ἀνδρῶν πόθῳ [and beds with longing for men]"}, {"id": "pothos-note4", "translation": "Πόθῳ [with longing]"}, {"id": "pothos-note5", "translation": "Πόθῳ δ᾽ ὑπερποντίας φάσμα δόξει δόμων [and with longing a phantom of the halls beyond the sea will seem]"}, {"id": "pothos-note6", "translation": "Μετάκοινοι δὲ φίλᾳ ματρὶ [and sharing the house with dear mother]"}, {"id": "pothos-note7", "translation": "Βενερι [to Venus]"}, {"id": "pothos-note8", "translation": "See Thes. vol. 6 p. 1286."}, {"id": "pothos-quote1", "translation": "may he cease from longing"}, {"id": "pothos-quote2", "translation": "groans with fierce"}, {"id": "pothos-quote3", "translation": "is filled with tears"}, {"id": "pothos-quote4", "translation": "husband-loving"}, {"id": "pothos-quote5", "translation": "to rule"}, {"id": "pothos-quote6", "translation": "there is Longing, to whom nothing is denied, with enchanting Persuasion"}, {"id": "pothos-word1", "translation": "so that the divine eye"}, {"id": "pothos-word2", "translation": "with longing"}, {"id": "pothos-word3", "translation": "and beds with longing for men"}, {"id": "pothos-word4", "translation": "with longing"}, {"id": "pothos-word5", "translation": "and with longing a phantom of the halls beyond the sea will seem"}, {"id": "pothos-word6", "translation": "Longing"}, {"id": "pothos-word7", "translation": "and sharing the house with dear mother"}, {"id": "pothos-word8", "translation": "to Venus"}, {"id": "poi-orth1", "translation": "where?"}, {"id": "poi-def1", "translation": "where?"}, {"id": "poi-note1", "translation": "Ἰὼ ἰὼ πόποι, | [Alas, alas, O gods!]"}, {"id": "poi-note2", "translation": "Thus corrected with Seidler, who reads in M ἰὼ ἰὼ ποῖ ποῖ ᾿πό ποι πό πὸι πῆ μ᾿ ἄγουσι – . τηλέπλαγκτοι πλάνοι? [alas, alas, where, where, from where, where, where, where are they leading me? – far-wandering wanderings?]"}, {"id": "poi-note3", "translation": "Ποῖ ποτ᾽ [where ever?]"}, {"id": "poi-note4", "translation": "Where then [do you bring] me, wretched me, here?"}, {"id": "poi-note5", "translation": "Where then"}, {"id": "poi-note6", "translation": "Where [is] this wave"}, {"id": "poi-note7", "translation": "Where"}, {"id": "poi-note8", "translation": "And where, having advanced to the end"}, {"id": "poi-note9", "translation": "And how then"}, {"id": "poi-note10", "translation": "Where"}, {"id": "poi-note11", "translation": "And where does it end and"}, {"id": "poi-note12", "translation": "Where then will it accomplish, where will the transferred might cease"}, {"id": "poi-note13", "translation": "Where"}, {"id": "poi-note14", "translation": "Where, where indeed of the nether gods"}, {"id": "poi-note15", "translation": "Where"}, {"id": "poi-note16", "translation": "[Where, forward, where.]"}, {"id": "poi-quote1", "translation": "Where are they leading me—far-wandering wanderings?"}, {"id": "poi-quote2", "translation": "Did you lead me?"}, {"id": "poi-quote3", "translation": "Did you lead?"}, {"id": "poi-quote4", "translation": "Do you tread?"}, {"id": "poi-quote5", "translation": "Will he lead away?"}, {"id": "poi-quote6", "translation": "Should we flee from the land of Apia?"}, {"id": "poi-quote7", "translation": "Will a god bring it upon?"}, {"id": "poi-quote8", "translation": "Where to end?"}, {"id": "poi-quote9", "translation": "Do you overturn the end of words?"}, {"id": "poi-quote10", "translation": "Is the word being accomplished?"}, {"id": "poi-quote11", "translation": "Of ruin?"}, {"id": "poi-quote12", "translation": "Has the end been ordained?"}, {"id": "poi-quote13", "translation": "Tyrannies?"}, {"id": "poi-quote14", "translation": "Clytemnestra?"}, {"id": "poi-word1", "translation": "Alas, alas, O gods"}, {"id": "poi-word2", "translation": "Thus corrected by Seidler, who reads in M: ἰὼ ἰὼ ποῖ ποῖ ᾿πό ποι πό πὸι πῆ μ᾿ ἄγουσι – . τηλέπλαγκτοι πλάνοι [Alas, alas, where, where, to where, where, where, where are they leading me—far-wandering wanderings]"}, {"id": "poi-word3", "translation": "Where ever"}, {"id": "poi-word4", "translation": "Where then [do you bring] me, wretched me, here?"}, {"id": "poi-word5", "translation": "Where then"}, {"id": "poi-word6", "translation": "Where [is] this wave"}, {"id": "poi-word7", "translation": "Where"}, {"id": "poi-word8", "translation": "And where, having advanced to the end"}, {"id": "poi-word9", "translation": "And how then"}, {"id": "poi-word10", "translation": "Where"}, {"id": "poi-word11", "translation": "And where does it end and"}, {"id": "poi-word12", "translation": "Where then will it accomplish, where will the transferred might cease"}, {"id": "poi-word13", "translation": "Where"}, {"id": "poi-word14", "translation": "Where, where indeed of the nether gods"}, {"id": "poi-word15", "translation": "Where"}, {"id": "poi-word16", "translation": "Where forward where"}, {"id": "poieo-orth1", "translation": "to do, make"}, {"id": "poieo-def1", "translation": "I do, make."}, {"id": "poieo-note1", "translation": "Κίο. Ὁ δ᾽ [And he]"}, {"id": "poieo-note2", "translation": "Τοὺς δ᾽ ἕν τι [And them one thing]"}, {"id": "poieo-note3", "translation": "Σθένος δὲ [And strength]"}, {"id": "poieo-note4", "translation": "Τούτων ἐπῳδὰς οὐκ [Not incantations of these]"}, {"id": "poieo-note5", "translation": "Οὗτος τί [This one what]"}, {"id": "poieo-note6", "translation": "Ὄρνιθα δ᾽ οὐ [And not a bird]"}, {"id": "poieo-note7", "translation": "Ὄξους σπανίζειν δῶμα [The house to lack vinegar]"}, {"id": "poieo-note8", "translation": "which Plutarch quotes in Mor. p. 632f, inserted into his own words, so that it is not clear whether Aeschylus used this very word ποιήσαντας [having done] or another."}, {"id": "poieo-quote1", "translation": "Therefore let him do"}, {"id": "poieo-quote2", "translation": "to do, but I say that they do nothing"}, {"id": "poieo-quote3", "translation": "to make your pledge good"}, {"id": "poieo-quote4", "translation": "my father made"}, {"id": "poieo-quote5", "translation": "Do you do?"}, {"id": "poieo-quote6", "translation": "I make you [lord] of my way"}, {"id": "poieo-quote7", "translation": "having done"}, {"id": "poieo-word1", "translation": "And he"}, {"id": "poieo-word2", "translation": "And them one thing"}, {"id": "poieo-word3", "translation": "And strength"}, {"id": "poieo-word4", "translation": "Not incantations of these"}, {"id": "poieo-word5", "translation": "This one what"}, {"id": "poieo-word6", "translation": "And not a bird"}, {"id": "poieo-word7", "translation": "The house to lack vinegar"}, {"id": "poieo-word8", "translation": "having done"}, {"id": "poikileimon-orth1", "translation": "wearing a variegated garment"}, {"id": "poikileimon-def1", "translation": "clothed in a variegated garment."}, {"id": "poikileimon-note1", "translation": "Ἡ [She]"}]}